  "cover_text": "In a small bowl, combine fennel, capers, gremolata, gouda, salt and pepper. Mix with a hand mixer and let sit for 20-30 minutes to allow herbs to blend.\nTap the colander on a damp, lined board or screen to separate the fennel from the liquid.\nMildly steam the fennel with cooking spray or olive oil in a fraction of an inch deep, for a light shine. Do not boil, as it will start to swell and become drier.\nWhen done, rinse thoroughly with water. Strain into a salad bowl, gently shaking off excess sugars, i.e., as it tastes.\nStick a fork into the tassels to make sure they are tender to",
